# PHASE 4: RELEASE HARDENING (server, PWA, performance, accessibility, SEO)

- **Server (`server.ts`).** Security headers (HSTS, `X-Content-Type-Options`, `Referrer-Policy`, `Permissions-Policy: camera=(self)`), CSP in **Report-Only first**; no restrictive `frame-ancestors` unless you have confirmed how AI Studio embeds the app. `Cache-Control: immutable` for hashed `/assets/*`, `no-cache` for `index.html`, `sw.js`, `manifest.webmanifest`. Unknown asset paths return **404**, not the SPA HTML with 200. JSON request logging (no query strings or tokens), error middleware (no stack traces), graceful shutdown on `SIGTERM`, `trust proxy`, compression, `/api/health` returns only `{status}`.
- **Service worker.** Versioned cache name injected at build time, delete old caches on activate, never cache `text/html` as an asset, cap runtime cache, network-first navigations, "New version available — Refresh" instead of silent mid-session `skipWaiting`.
- **Performance targets (mobile, 4G):** LCP ≤ 2.5 s, INP ≤ 200 ms, CLS ≤ 0.1, initial JS ≤ 250 KB gzip (about 292 KB now), check-in round trip p95 ≤ 1.5 s, Firestore reads per active member ≤ 100 per hour. Bound admin listeners (recent months by default, "load all history" on demand). Memoize stats computation. Report chunk sizes before and after.
- **Accessibility.** `aria-live` / `role="alert"` for scanner results, confirmation, loading and errors (none exist today); label the error-banner close button; contrast check of `text-zinc-500/600` on dark backgrounds (WCAG AA); `prefers-reduced-motion` coverage for every CSS animation; focus-visible rings; 44 px targets; labels and `autocomplete` on forms.
- **SEO and metadata.** Unique `document.title` per route, `robots` meta (index only the public leaderboard/landing), canonical, `og:*` and Twitter tags with an absolute image URL, `robots.txt`, `<noscript>`, complete manifest. Make `/#/leaderboard` open for signed-out visitors.
- **Environment.** `VITE_PUBLIC_BASE_URL` must be the canonical published URL so QR codes created in the AI Studio preview do not point at the preview origin. Warn in the kiosk if the origin looks like a preview. Update the README (remove the stale `GEMINI_API_KEY` instruction).
- **Observability.** `POST /api/client-error` (≤ 4 KB, in-memory rate limit) writing JSON log lines to stdout; client logger sends sanitized errors only. Add an `APP_VERSION` constant shown in the footer and sent as a response header.
- **CI.** `.github/workflows/ci.yml`: install, lint, tests, rules tests on the emulator, build.

